  "description": "Injury and condition concepts. Unlike the other four vocabularies this one is not enumerable from the catalog - the sample member has exactly one injury, and the whole point is that the system must handle the next one too. The set below covers the sample member's condition plus the musculoskeletal presentations a coach-facing product will actually meet, chosen so that every one of the 9 catalog joints has at least one condition anchored to it.",
  "coverage": "16 conditions. 15 reach a skos:exactMatch in SNOMED CT; the sixteenth (cond_rotator_cuff_syndrome) reaches only a closeMatch, because SNOMED has no unlateralised concept for it. Every code verified against NCI EVS snomedct_us 2025_09_01. Every condition carries an anatomy_anchor into anatomy-partonomy.json, which is what connects it to the catalog by traversal.",
  "anchor_semantics": "anatomy_anchor is the most specific structure the condition is about. The safety closure walks upward from there through PART_OF / IS_A, and at each ancestor may also take a single PART_OF step back down, until it reaches a catalog-tagged joint. The optional down-step is what lets a tendon or muscle condition reach the joint it shares a region with: the rotator cuff is part of the shoulder region but not part of the shoulder joint, so upward-only traversal would never connect a cuff problem to shoulder-loading exercises. reaches_catalog_joint_via records which of the two routes each condition takes.",
