  "known_gaps": [
    "hip and thoracic spine have no condition anchored to them. Both are catalog joints (25 and 2 exercises respectively), so a hip or thoracic complaint currently degrades to the blunt joint-level filter rather than to a mechanics-aware rule. Femoroacetabular impingement and thoracic facet irritation are the obvious next two to curate.",
    "No condition here is a systemic or cardiometabolic one. The sample member's lab panel is in scope for the copilot but not for the movement graph, and modelling e.g. uncontrolled hypertension as a contraindication to heavy axial loading would need clinical sign-off this exercise cannot supply."
  ]
